# The maintenance job: look at Qdrant, heal what can be healed, and leave a record for health.
#
# Started every 15 minutes by wiki-mirror-maintain.timer (and by hand: `systemctl start
# wiki-mirror-maintain`). `python -m wiki_mirror maintain` asks Qdrant how each mirror collection
# is, and reads systemd's view of wiki-mirror-qdrant.service (restarts after a failure, memory
# against its cap). It then:
#   * resumes a collection whose status is `grey` - Qdrant 1.12 does not restart pending
#     optimizations after it is restarted (an OOM kill, 2026-10-23) until some update arrives, so
#     the job sends the empty update that starts them;
#   * keeps the semantic collection's storage and optimizer settings equal to what the code
#     declares (a storage change makes Qdrant rebuild the graphs in the background);
#   * writes <data_dir>/state/maintenance.json, which /v1/wiki/health and `wiki-mirror status`
#     read. Health says `degraded` when the record is more than an hour old: four missed runs.
# It never starts, retries or touches an embedding run, a build or an update.
#
# Runs as `wikimirror-sync`, the build user, because it needs to write the record where the other
# jobs write their state, and the API user must not be able to write the data (CLAUDE.md,
# constraint 6). It uses nothing but Qdrant on loopback (nftables already lets this user do so,
# as the embed unit does) and the local state directory; it holds no credentials and needs no
# network beyond loopback.
#
# **Safe to run unattended, on every box.** It only reads, resumes and applies the code's own
# settings; every action is idempotent, so a run that is killed half way costs the next run a
# repeat, nothing more.
#
# **It never takes the build lock.** A build or an embedding run holds it for hours or days, and
# that is exactly when Qdrant is busiest and most likely to fall over; the job must still run
# then. It touches no build or index state, only Qdrant's own settings and its own record.
#
# **Qdrant down is a result, not a failure.** `After=` orders it behind Qdrant at boot, but there
# is no `Requires=`: with Qdrant stopped the job must still run, write a record that says so, and
# let health report it. Exit 1 means the record could not be written; the next run is the retry,
# so no Restart= here - the timer is the retry.
#
# systemd access: the job runs `systemctl show` (over D-Bus, so AF_UNIX stays in
# RestrictAddressFamilies and /run stays readable) and reads /sys/fs/cgroup/.../memory.stat and
# memory.max, which stay readable under ProtectControlGroups=true (that makes them read-only,
# which is all it needs).
#
# 256 M: a Python process with the Qdrant client holds about 100 MB. TimeoutStartSec=5min is far
# above a run (a few seconds); a hang is cut and the next quarter hour tries again.
#
# `-I` (isolated mode) for the same reason as the API unit.
#
# Install: install.sh copies it and enables wiki-mirror-maintain.timer. A box that updates itself
# gets the unit from update.sh but not the timer: enable it once with
# `systemctl enable --now wiki-mirror-maintain.timer`. See docs/DESIGN.md section 12.5 and
# docs/OPERATIONS.md ("The maintenance job").

[Unit]
Description=Wikipedia mirror maintenance (heal Qdrant, record what was seen)
Documentation=file:///opt/wiki-mirror/docs/OPERATIONS.md
After=wiki-mirror-qdrant.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=wikimirror-sync
Group=wikimirror
WorkingDirectory=/var/lib/wiki-mirror
ExecStart=/opt/wiki-mirror/.venv/bin/python -I -m wiki_mirror maintain
# Group-readable output (the API user is in group wikimirror and reads the record), nothing for
# anyone else.
UMask=0027

TimeoutStartSec=5min
Nice=10
IOSchedulingClass=idle
MemoryMax=256M

# Hardening, as the embed unit's. One writable place: local data. It talks to Qdrant on
# loopback and to systemd over its socket.
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
PrivateDevices=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=true
ProtectKernelTunables=true
ProtectKernelModules=true
ProtectControlGroups=true
RestrictSUIDSGID=true
RestrictRealtime=true
RestrictNamespaces=true
LockPersonality=true
SystemCallArchitectures=native
CapabilityBoundingSet=
ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/wiki-mirror
RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_INET AF_INET6 AF_UNIX
